<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00284</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7f0c1e43-4446-40b0-b452-fbcdc7480130</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will not only write equations given a point and slope or two points but also from verbal descriptions and from tables.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Write equations from a point and slope.</item>
        <item>Write equations from two points.</item>
        <item>Write equations from a verbal description.</item>
        <item>Write equations from a table.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>1.13.1: Writing Linear Equations</item>
        <item>1.13.2: Creating Tables from Verbal Descriptions <list id="list-00003">
            <item>1.13.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.13.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>1.13.3: Matching Tables, Equations, and Graphs <list id="list-00004">
            <item>1.13.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.13.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>1.13.4: Creating a Table from an Equation</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>1.13.5: Practice</item>
        <item>1.13.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
